==English==

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-proper noun|head=[[immaculate|Immaculate]] [[conception|Conception]]}}

# The [[doctrine]], in the [[Roman Catholic Church]], that the [[Virgin Mary]] was [[conceive]]d free from [[original sin]]
# December 8th (The ''Feast of the Immaculate Conception of Mary'')
# {{cx|proscribed|lang=en}} The conception of [[Jesus]] as viewed by those who believe that he was conceived without sin.

====Usage notes====
* Usage referring to the conception of Jesus rather than that of Mary is based on ignorance or misunderstanding of the original term and of the doctrine it refers to, but it is nonetheless relatively widespread.

